 // monthly downloads and recency is the package date. Nothing reads pi.dev.
 //
+// A Piglet published with `pig piglet publish --to npm` may record its signed Binary release in package.json
+// (`pig.binaries`: { ref, signer }). npm search results do not carry that field, so the build reads the published
+// package.json of each listed Piglet from the registry and keeps `binaries` on the entry when both values are well
+// formed. The cards then show `pig piglet pull <ref>` next to `pig piglet add npm:<name>`. A Piglet whose package.json
+// cannot be read keeps the saved value when its version is unchanged; it never fails the build.
+//
 // A source that cannot be fetched completely (any page fails after retries,
 // or the result shrinks below half of the saved snapshot) keeps the saved
 // snapshot in data/npm-catalog.snapshot.json, never an empty or partial list.
